4. Interpretation (Chemical Meaning Only)

Positive oxygen balance means the molecule contains more oxygen than required to oxidize its carbon and hydrogen.

This is a purely compositional statement derived from elemental stoichiometry.

It does not by itself imply any specific physical behavior or application.

